    "repository": "https://github.com/git/git/blob/v2.51.1/builtin/update-index.c",
    "source_blob": "2380f3ccd68c8ce0ac4b221dbf84f18b9a430811",
    "reason": "update_one returns before reading working-file content when assume-unchanged is explicitly set or cleared; the outer loop then calls chmod_path. Match the existing tag case to preserve that flag. Do not use bare update-index --chmod or git add for a mode-only repair."
  },
  "contract": [
    "Read NUL-delimited staged entries. Only extensionless basenames under .githooks are subjects, including nested entries.",
    "Require stage zero and mode 100755. Fail empty audits, unmerged entries and unsupported repair modes.",
    "The native PowerShell adapter retains the existing shared mutex, index-lock wait and retry coordinator. The normal staging path is unchanged.",
    "Repair only executable modes; preserve staged blobs and assume-unchanged, skip-worktree and intent-to-add settings. Verify readback before success and respect the active alternate index and other writers locks.",
    "Keep noncooperating index writers idle. This is not a compare-and-swap across the Python census, coordinator and readback. A failed readback after mutation requires inspection before retry; no rollback is claimed.",
    "Git reads have 30-second deadlines. Index mutation retains the native coordinator lifecycle; no parent deadline is imposed around an in-flight shared index write."
  ],
  "native_exception": "The existing PowerShell/.NET process mutex and retry coordinator remains a justified host boundary shared with other index writers. Hook selection, index parsing, validation and final readback run in typed Python. Current flag reads and native argument construction stay inside the native critical section. No replacement locking architecture is introduced.",
